        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Are Iran's retaliatory strikes across the Gulf region affecting the US' war strategy? Middle East Issued on: 15/03/2026 - 14:54 Israel's military said it began a broad wave of strikes on western Iran on Sunday. As the war progresses into the third week, further retaliatory strikes from Iran are likely to occur. So far, Iran has launched strikes across nine countries in the Gulf region. Most of these attacks have been intercepted but at least 19 people have been killed. The US and Israel started this war but it seems the Gulf states are bearing the brunt of Iran's retaliation. Could this affect the United States' strategy in the war? Analysis by Joe Macaron, geopolitical analyst and non-resident association researcher at the Arab World Institute in Paris. Trump urges allies to send warships to Strait of Hormuz 15/03/2026 Middle East Could Nigeria become an alternative oil supplier to the Middle East? 15/03/2026 Africa Who is running Iran? The regime's new strongmen 15/03/2026 Middle East What role is oil playing in the war in the Middle East and what's at stake? 15/03/2026 Analysis Middle East Gaza hit by strongest sandstorm in over five years 15/03/2026 Middle East Qatar, Kuwait, UAE... Iranian reprisals disrupt daily life across the Gulf 15/03/2026 Middle East Undercover in Iran: How French spies gather Intelligence in the Middle East 15/03/2026 Middle East Israel pounds Beirut, deepening the humanitarian crisis in Lebanon 15/03/2026 Middle East Donald Trump says will open Strait of Hormuz \"one way or another\" 15/03/2026 Middle East"
