        "contenuto_esteso": "Saturday Night Live hilariously targeted Timothée Chalamet's recent remarks on opera and ballet during its cold open. Portraying Donald Trump, James Austin Johnson quipped about Iran being like opera and ballet, a jab at Chalamet's comments about keeping dying art forms alive. The skit also touched on rising gas prices and campaign promises, with Colin Jost appearing as Pete Hegseth."
